      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. CIII.—मनोरथोपरचितप्रासाद is equivalent to castle in the air.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "The Stanza occurs at p. 301 of the Kâvyasangraha.—S'ârdûla-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "vikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. CIV.—आघ्रान is apparently used as a synonyme of ग्रस्त oc-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "curring in the fourth line. I observe that Râmarshi expressly",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "says ग्रस्तमित्यर्थः. The word is used in a similar sense in the Das'a-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "kumâracharita p. 11 (Calc. Ed. 1925 Sam.) विद्युच्चलं यौवनम् it will be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "seen breaks the symmetry of the Stanza, but none of the variants",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "preserve it. उपहता is a better reading than अपहृता. वा इति आश्चर्ये says",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "Râmarshi. But see our note to Nîtis'ataka St. 32.—S'ârdûla-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "vikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. CV.—आधिव्याधि may be taken as a Dvandva. In the Mâlatî-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "Mâdhava (p. 145) where the expression occurs it is explained by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "Jagaddhara as आधय एव व्याधयः; unnecessarily, I think. Construe यत्र",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "लक्ष्मीस्तत्र आपदः पतन्ति—आपद् is not a very usual form but occurs",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "in Mṛichchhakaṭika p. 213 (Calc. Ed.) आत्मसात्. See Siddh. Kaum.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "I., 731. तत्किं नाम &c. “and what indeed is there which unbridled",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "destiny has created well-constituted.”—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. CVI.—नियमित = cramped, compressed. The second line as it",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "stands in our text is explained by both commentators, but it cer-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "tainly seems to involve a pleonasm. “In youth which is painful",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "through separation there is separation.” The reading of Bo.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "and N. would seem to be better. “The enjoyments of youth are",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "painful by reason of the grief of separation.” नारीणामप्यवज्ञा is taken",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "by the commentator with the second line and to this construc-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "tion the two अपि would seem to give support. Râmarshi's read-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "ing is somewhat different and he takes the whole line as one con-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "struing असाधुः with अवज्ञा. This I think is better. See St. 111. As",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "it stands the first अपि may be taken as meaning again, and इत्यतः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "or some expression of like import must be supplied after विलसति.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
